        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(durable): expose wake inspection",
        "body": "# PR4/5 - inspection-first durable wake observability\n\n## Context capsule\n\nThis PR is item 4 of the rebuilt beta3 durable core stack. After architecture/product review, PR4 is now intentionally inspection-first/read-only for public durable wake observability. Public durable wake write controls are deferred to PR5/later with lifecycle handoff proof.\n\n## Durable core stack overview\n\n- PR1/5 - docs/RFC/boundary anchor.\n- PR2/5 - runtime foundation/core plus terminal SQLite row immutability guard.\n- PR3/5 - wake targets, durable producers, replay/resume semantics.\n- PR4/5 - public durable wake inspection/observability plus CLI/Gateway/API read paths.\n- PR5/5 - internal session delivery handoff, final hardening, and any reviewed write-control contract.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nPR3 persists durable wake obligations and delivery attempts. Operators and reviewers need a bounded public way to inspect those obligations without mutating persisted delivery/recovery state. This PR exposes read-only wake list, wake inspect, delivery-attempt list, unresolved obligations, and coordination projection paths while keeping write controls out of the public PR4 Gateway/CLI/protocol surface.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Public Gateway/CLI/protocol inspection paths:\n  - `durable.coordination.get`\n  - `durable.obligations.list`\n  - `durable.wake.list`\n  - `durable.wake.inspect`\n  - `durable.wake.deliveryAttempts.list`\n- Public durable wake write controls removed/deferred:\n  - `durable.wake.acknowledge`\n  - `durable.wake.supersede`\n  - `durable.wake.mark`\n  - CLI `wake-ack`, `wake-supersede`, `wake-mark`\n- Generated Swift protocol models updated to remove deferred write params/result.\n- Shipped plugin SDK compatibility preserved for `NodeSession` from `openclaw/plugin-sdk/gateway-runtime` with external packaged consumer proof.\n\n## Non-scope\n\n- No public durable wake mutation controls in PR4.\n- No external transport delivery claim.\n- No PR5 promotion.\n- No cron changes.\n\n## Architecture rationale\n\nPublic wake writes can terminalize persisted obligations and affect recovery/message delivery. PR4 keeps the public contract inspection-first so operators can diagnose durable state without creating compatibility expectations around write authorization, idempotency, terminal-state rejection, audit semantics, or lifecycle/session delivery handoff. Internal store write primitives remain available for PR5 integration but are not exposed as PR4 public API.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Final head: `d7857aa47459c23e89fca642061b43010d5eeeb7`\n- Head before implementation: `8856c95432bf3ab2b343a3896ee18362d25eaabf`\n- Detailed proof artifact: `/Users/avo/aicos/runtime/openclaw-durable-pr-stack/pr4-inspection-first-implementation-proof-2026-07-13.md`\n- Focused tests: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs packages/gateway-protocol/src/index.test.ts src/gateway/server-methods/durable.test.ts src/commands/durable.test.ts test/release-check.test.ts` passed, 4 shards / 127 tests.\n- Plugin SDK dts/export proof: `pnpm build:plugin-sdk:dts && node --import tsx scripts/write-plugin-sdk-entry-dts.ts && node scripts/check-plugin-sdk-exports.mjs` passed; declaration graph 4,389,302 bytes under 5,000,000 byte cap; `gateway-runtime.d.ts` includes `NodeSession`.\n- Plugin SDK surface/API: `pnpm plugin-sdk:surface:check` and `pnpm plugin-sdk:api:check` passed.\n- Protocol build: `pnpm --dir packages/gateway-protocol build` passed.\n- External packaged consumer smoke: packed `openclaw-2026.7.1-beta.6.tgz`, typechecked `import type { NodeSession } from \"openclaw/plugin-sdk/gateway-runtime\"`, loaded packaged `dist/plugin-sdk/gateway-runtime.js`, and called `errorShape(ErrorCodes.INVALID_REQUEST, ...)`; passed.\n- Lint/static fallback: `node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs <changed TS files>` passed; `git diff --check` passed.\n- Public-surface scan: only negative tests reference removed durable wake write names.\n\n## Proof gaps / environment notes\n\n- Remote Testbox proof was attempted but blocked because the local `blacksmith` executable is missing. AWS Crabbox warmup was also blocked by missing broker login. Focused local fallback proof was run and recorded.\n- `pnpm check:changed` delegates to the same unavailable Blacksmith backend in this worktree and was blocked for that reason.\n- Plain package-manager install of the root tarball in a temp consumer is currently blocked by the package's `@openclaw/ai@workspace:*` dependency resolution. The external consumer smoke therefore used the packed root artifact unpacked into external `node_modules/openclaw` plus installed declared runtime dependencies to prove the packaged subpath type/load behavior.\n\n## ClawSweeper review focus\n\nPlease review this PR as inspection-first/read-only public durable wake observability. Public write controls are intentionally deferred; findings should treat public `acknowledge`, `supersede`, or `mark` exposure in PR4 as a regression, not a missing feature.\n",
        "branch": "codex/openclaw-durable-beta3-newstack-pr4-controls-cli-gateway",
